# LEASH-151: the image must build from the repository, not from whatever the developer happens to have
# installed. Without this, `COPY solution/app/ ./` ships the host's node_modules (150+ MB) over the
# layer `npm ci` just produced, so the artifact APP_REVISION labels is not the one the lockfile
# describes — and every build drags the context along with it.
**/node_modules/
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/*.egg-info/
solution/app/dist/
solution/app/test-results/
solution/app/playwright-report/
solution/training/data/
.git/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
